# Neo Exciter parameters (docs/specs/mastering-tools.md §5.8). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoExciter
namespace NeoBuzz.Exciter
class NeoExciterMachine
summary Harmonic exciter, the successor of Oomek Exciter: up to four Linkwitz–Riley bands, each driven through an oversampled, anti-aliased shaper (tape, tube, transistor, diode, or warm: even harmonics only), and only the harmonics it makes (the shaper's output minus the audio) are added back, by an Amount per band. A band at 0 % is left alone, bit for bit. A high shelf on the added harmonics, optional auto gain, left/right or mid/side, Delta (hear only what it adds) and a gain-match reading. Use it for air and presence on masters, vocals and drum buses, or for warmth in the lows with Warm mode.

group Exciter
Mode       "Mode"         0 4     0     enum Tape Tube Transistor Diode Warm | The curve: Tape (tanh, odd harmonics), Tube (asymmetric, even and odd), Transistor (towards a hard clip), Diode (soft logarithmic, asymmetric), Warm (even harmonics only)
    how Chooses the curve that creates the added harmonics: Tape, Tube, Transistor, Diode or Warm.
    sound Tape and Tube sound smooth and rich, Transistor is bolder, Diode is edgy and Warm adds only even, full-sounding harmonics.
Drive      "Drive"        0 360   120   db 0 36                          | Gain into the shaper (before its output is brought back), 0.1 dB steps. More drive, more harmonics, higher orders
    how Raises the level into the harmonic generator by 0 to 36 dB.
    sound More drive creates more, and higher, harmonics for a brighter, more present sound.
group Bands
Xo1        "Crossover 1"  0 10000 5340  freq 20 20000                      | Between the first and the second band
    how Sets the frequency between the first and second band, from 20 Hz to 20 kHz.
    sound It decides where the lowest band, usually left alone, ends.
Xo2        "Crossover 2"  0 10000 7253  freq 20 20000                      | Between the second and the third band (never below Crossover 1)
    how Sets the frequency between the second and third band.
    sound It moves the boundary between the lower and upper midrange for excitation.
Xo3        "Crossover 3"  0 10000 8674  freq 20 20000                      | Between the third and the fourth band (never below Crossover 2)
    how Sets the frequency between the third and fourth band.
    sound It decides where the topmost band, which usually carries the air, begins.
Amount1    "Amount 1"     0 1000  0     pct                                | How much of the first band's harmonics is added. 0 % leaves the band alone
    how Sets how much harmonic content is added to the first band, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Above 0 the lows gain weight and warmth; at 0 they are left untouched.
Amount2    "Amount 2"     0 1000  0     pct                                | The second band's Amount
    how Sets how much harmonic content is added to the second band.
    sound More adds body and warmth to the low midrange.
Amount3    "Amount 3"     0 1000  0     pct                                | The third band's Amount
    how Sets how much harmonic content is added to the third band.
    sound More adds presence and bite to the upper midrange.
Amount4    "Amount 4"     0 1000  250   pct                                | The fourth band's Amount
    how Sets how much harmonic content is added to the fourth band.
    sound More adds shine and air to the top end.
group Output
ShelfFreq  "Shelf freq"   0 10000 6942  freq 1000 20000                    | The corner of the high shelf on the added harmonics
    how Sets the corner of a high shelf that shapes only the added harmonics, from 1 to 20 kHz.
    sound It decides where the added sparkle starts to be boosted or softened.
ShelfGain  "Shelf gain"   0 240   120   db -12 12                          | The high shelf's gain on the added harmonics: brighter or duller excitation without touching the audio
    how Sets the high shelf's gain on the added harmonics, from -12 to +12 dB.
    sound Positive values make the excitation brighter, negative values make it duller, without changing the original audio.
Auto       "Auto gain"    0 1     0     switch                             | Keeps the loudness: the output's level (300 ms) follows the input's, within ±6 dB
    how Keeps the loudness steady by following the input level within 6 dB.
    sound You hear the added brightness rather than a louder sound.
Stereo     "Stereo"       0 1     0     enum L/R M/S                       | What is excited: left and right, or mid and side (harmonics of the side widen, of the mid centre)
    how Chooses whether harmonics are added to left and right, or to mid and side.
    sound Mid/side adds harmonics to the sides to widen the sound, or to the centre to focus it.
Output     "Output"       0 480   240   db -24 24                          | Gain after the exciter, 0.1 dB steps (the editor's Match sets it from the gain-match reading)
    how Adds -24 to +24 dB of gain after the exciter.
    sound It matches the loudness to the dry sound so you judge the added tone fairly.
Delta      "Delta"        0 1     0     switch                             | Hear only what the exciter adds: the output minus the input, delayed to match (glides over 10 ms)
    how Plays only the difference between the output and the input.
    sound You hear only the harmonics that the exciter adds.

# What the exciter measures (NeoExciterMachine.Readings, machine_readings), over the last 3 s.
reading added_db          dB    | Level of the added harmonics against the input (RMS, dB); −100 when nothing is added
reading gain_match_db     dB    | Short-term loudness out − in (K-weighted, 3 s): what Output would have to take back for equal loudness
reading latency_samples   samples | The oversampling's delay, constant, reported to NeoBuzz Live
